WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
A launcher on flat ground
fires a ball at thirty degrees.

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:07.060
Then the same speed at sixty degrees.

3
00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.640
The steep throw hangs in the air longer.

4
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.210
The flat one moves forwards faster.

5
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.300
They land in the same spot.

6
00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:16.800
So what angle throws furthest?

7
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.980
And from shoulder height,
is it the same angle?

8
00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.930
In this mission, you'll
split the motion in two:

9
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.980
constant speed horizontally, and
acceleration g downwards vertically.

10
00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.730
The vertical motion
gives the time of flight.

11
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.080
Horizontal speed times
that time gives the range.

12
00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:38.430
And you'll see what changes when the
launch point is above the landing point.

13
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.590
Your mission: find the
angle that throws furthest,

14
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.890
and explain why real throws differ.
